 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20SP%20%20MATHEMATICS%20GR%207-9.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Calculate the percentage of part of a whole; calculate percentage increase or decrease; solve problems in contexts involving percentages.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 7 percentages worksheets: percentages of amounts, multipliers, percentage increase and decrease and one amount as a percentage. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Per cent means out of 100.",
 "key_sub": "Increase by 20%: × 1,2.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Per cent means out of 100: 35% = 0,35.</li><li>Find 10% by dividing by 10, then build: 35% = 3 × 10% + 5%.</li><li>With a multiplier: 35% of R240 = 0,35 × R240 = R84.</li><li>Increase by 20%: × 1,2. Decrease by 20%: × 0,8.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Increase R450 by 12%</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>12% of R450 = R54</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: R504</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>5% as 0,5</td><td>5% = 0,05.</td></tr><tr><td>The increase, not the new amount</td><td>Add it on.</td></tr><tr><td>Dividing the wrong way</td><td>Part ÷ whole × 100.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 7 say about percentages?",
   "a": "Calculate percentages of whole numbers, express one quantity as a percentage of another, and find percentage increase and decrease."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 25% of 80?",
   "a": "20."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 18 out of 24 as a percentage?",
   "a": "75%."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is a multiplier?",
   "a": "The decimal you multiply by, like 0,35 for 35%."
  }
